# Project License Compliance Report

> Generated: 2026-05-15
> Audit guide: https://tpscsm-docs.pages.dev/license-audit/
> This report is for compliance reference only and is not legal advice.

## Project License

Project SPDX baseline: `GPL-3.0-only`

Rationale: this codebase imports `PyQt6` and `PyQt6-WebEngine`. Their PyPI
open-source distribution path is `GPL-3.0-only`, with a Riverbank commercial
license available as an alternative. For a public GitHub release without a
documented commercial PyQt entitlement, `GPL-3.0-only` is the compatible
open-source baseline.

The short project license notice is stored in `COPYING`. Before a public
release, the project owner should confirm the copyright holder name and whether
the repository should include the full GPL-3.0 license text.

## Copyright License Compliance Conclusion

Final assessment: compliant for open-source distribution if the repository and
release artifacts are distributed under `GPL-3.0-only` and include source,
license, and third-party notices.

Important boundary: the same dependency set is not compatible with an MIT,
Apache-2.0, or proprietary-only project license unless the project owner has and
documents a valid Riverbank commercial license for PyQt/PyQt-WebEngine.

## Distribution Obligations

- Distribute the complete corresponding source for the released application.
- Keep `GPL-3.0-only` project license notice visible in the repository and
  release package.
- Preserve third-party license notices for PyQt6, PyQt6-WebEngine, requests,
  playwright, and any packaged browser/runtime data.
- If FFmpeg GPL binaries are bundled, include FFmpeg notices and source-offer
  information; if the app only downloads FFmpeg on demand, document that the
  user obtains FFmpeg from the upstream provider.
- Do not impose additional downstream restrictions that conflict with GPL-3.0.

## Dependency License Summary

| Category | Count | Result |
| --- | ---: | --- |
| Strong copyleft (`GPL-3.0-only`) | 2 | Compatible with GPL-3.0-only project baseline |
| Permissive (`Apache-2.0`) | 2 | Compatible with GPL-3.0-only project baseline; preserve notices |
| Unknown | 0 | None found |
| Non-open-source | 0 | None found |

## Compatibility Details

| Dependency | Dependency License | Compatibility With Project GPL-3.0-only | Distribution Duty |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| PyQt6 | GPL-3.0-only or commercial | Compatible under GPL-3.0-only | Release project under GPL-3.0-only unless commercial PyQt license is used |
| PyQt6-WebEngine | GPL-3.0-only or commercial | Compatible under GPL-3.0-only | Same PyQt commercial/GPL boundary; Riverbank states PyQt-WebEngine is not LGPL |
| requests | Apache-2.0 | Compatible | Preserve Apache-2.0 license and notices |
| playwright | Apache-2.0 | Compatible | Preserve Apache-2.0 license and notices; track bundled browser assets separately |

## Third-Party License Notices

### GPL-3.0-only

- `PyQt6==6.11.0` — Riverbank Computing Limited.
- `PyQt6-WebEngine==6.11.0` — Riverbank Computing Limited.

### Apache-2.0

- `requests==2.34.2` — Python Software Foundation / Requests maintainers.
- `playwright==1.59.0` — Microsoft Corporation.

## Risk Notes

1. PyQt6 and PyQt6-WebEngine are the decisive licensing factors. A permissive
   project license should not be used for public distribution unless commercial
   PyQt licensing is documented.
2. FFmpeg is currently fetched from a GPL build URL in `core.py`; avoid bundling
   that binary without notices and source-offer handling.
3. Re-run this audit whenever `requirements.txt`, `web_tools/package.json`, or
   the FFmpeg distribution strategy changes.
